# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust. Nothing here is a secret.

# The API's origin (arvent-backend). Used in exactly three places:
#   1. `next.config.ts`, which rewrites same-origin `/backend/*` to it.
#   2. The route proxy's `GET /auth/me` session check.
#   3. Link-preview `<meta>` tags.
#
# Deliberately NOT `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`: the browser bundle has no business knowing
# the API's hostname, and a full API URL in the bundle is what turns "logged in"
# into "logged out on the next page load" once web and API are different hosts.
#
# Point this at wherever arvent-backend runs — never at this web app. `next dev`
# serves this app on :3000, so the example uses :4000 for the API.
API_URL=http://localhost:4000

# This app's own address — the web app, never the API. Email templates and share
# links build absolute URLs from it. The web app serves on :3000.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
